SDDMS APP USAGE GUIDE
============================================================
NOTE FOR DEVELOPER: This file is the knowledge base the AI
Assistant chatbot uses to answer "how do I use the app /
where do I click" questions. Edit the sections below so the
button names, page names and steps match your ACTUAL frontend
screens. The AI will only be as accurate as this file.
============================================================


1. ACCOUNTS / LOGIN
------------------------------------------------------------
- New users register from the Register page (name, email,
  password). After registering, an admin/staff member must
  approve the account from the "Pending Verifications" page
  before the user can log in.
- Existing users log in from the Login page with email and
  password.
- A logged-in user can view/update their own profile from the
  "My Profile" page (top-right menu).
- Admins manage all users from the "Users" page: add new
  users, change a user's role, activate/deactivate accounts.


2. CASES
------------------------------------------------------------
- All cases are listed on the "Cases" page.
- To create a new case, click the "+ New Case" button, fill
  in the case details form, and click "Save".
- Click on any case row to open the case detail page, where
  you can see its complaints, documents, evidence, witness
  statements and AI analysis/summary in one place.
- Use the "Edit" button on the case detail page to update case
  information, or "Delete" to remove a case.


3. COMPLAINTS
------------------------------------------------------------
- Complaints are listed under a case's detail page (or under
  the "Complaints" page).
- Click "+ Add Complaint" to file a new complaint, fill the
  form, and click "Save".
- Click a complaint row to view or edit its details.


4. DOCUMENTS
------------------------------------------------------------
- Documents for a case are managed from the case's "Documents"
  tab.
- Click "Upload Document" to upload a new file. Choose the
  file, add a title/description, and click "Upload".
- Click a document to view its details, download it, see its
  version history, or upload a new version.
- Use "Share" to share a document with another user, or
  "Archive" to archive it.
- Use "Sign" to digitally sign a document, and "Verify
  Signature" / "Verify Integrity" to confirm it hasn't been
  tampered with.
- The "AI Analyze" and "AI Summarize" buttons on a case's
  documents tab generate an AI-written analysis or summary of
  all documents in that case.


5. EVIDENCE
------------------------------------------------------------
- Evidence items are listed under a case's "Evidence" tab.
- Click "+ Add Evidence" to log new evidence, fill in details
  (description, custody info), and click "Save".
- Click an evidence row to view its details or custody
  transfer history.


6. WITNESS STATEMENTS / INVESTIGATIONS
------------------------------------------------------------
- Investigations are listed under a case's "Investigation"
  tab.
- Click "+ Add Witness Statement" to record a new statement.
- The investigation history log shows every action taken
  during the investigation, in order.


7. LEGAL / COURT
------------------------------------------------------------
- Legal reviews and court hearings for a case are managed from
  the case's "Legal" tab.
- Click "+ Schedule Hearing" to add a new court hearing date.


8. AI FEATURES
------------------------------------------------------------
- On a case's page, "AI Analyze" and "AI Summarize" generate a
  plain-text analysis / summary of that case's documents.
- The "Ask AI Assistant" chat button (bottom-right corner on
  every page) opens this help chatbot, which can answer
  questions about how to use any part of the app.


GENERAL TIPS
------------------------------------------------------------
- Most list pages (Cases, Complaints, Evidence, Documents)
  follow the same pattern: a "+ Add" button top-right to create
  a new item, and clicking any row opens its details.
- Only Staff/Admin users can approve verifications, manage
  users, or change roles.